WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.150
We're constantly bombarded with trailers,
posters, and concept art for franchise films,

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.440
but there are a few big sequels coming out
that have stayed under the radar.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:12.420
From indie comedies to Biblical epics, let's
take a look at some of the sequels you didn't

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.420
know were being made.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:18.099
The Pirates of the Caribbean films have continued
to rake in money at the box office, but after

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.380
five movies, their appeal among audiences
and critics has been waning.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:27.519
The latest installment, 2017's Dead Men Tell
No Tales, sits at an abysmal 30% on Rotten

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:28.020
Tomatoes.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.399
It raises the question of whether more Pirates
sequels are warranted, but it looks like Disney

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.680
has decided to test the waters by dusting
off the franchise for at least one more outing.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:41.080
Ted Elliott, co-writer of the first four Pirates
movies, has been tapped to help come up with

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.980
a new adventure alongside Chernobyl scribe
Craig Mazin.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.500
Although this new Pirates film has been referred
to as a reboot, the writers and studio reportedly

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.200
haven't yet settled on a direction for the
sixth film.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.560
Among the questions still up in the air: whether
or not it will include Johnny Depp's swaggering,

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.740
hard-drinking character, Captain Jack Sparrow.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.760
"Well, today's your lucky day.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.940
'Cause I just happen to be Captain Jack Sparrow."

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.360
Despite Captain Jack's popularity, Johnny
Depp's Hollywood appeal has been on the decline

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:14.270
in recent years, bringing uncertainty as to
whether the studio will want to risk hanging

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:18.040
a fresh new Pirates tale on his shoulders,
or whether they'll opt to move on to a new

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:18.540
star.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:22.480
We'll have to wait to see whether the sixth
Pirates of the Caribbean is a sequel, reboot,

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:23.780
or something in between.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.420
Until then, drink up me hearties, yo ho.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.460
Although producer Phil Lord has said that
the team behind the Jump Street movies is

00:01:30.469 --> 00:01:35.610
putting a pin in 23 Jump Street, which would
mark the third outing for 21 and 22 Jump Street

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:40.950
stars Channing Tatum and Jonah Hill, the studio
is moving forward with a spinoff of the comedy

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.940
franchise, this time focusing on a female
duo.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:47.260
The first two Jump Street films followed a
pair of male cops who went undercover at educational

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.600
institutions in order to ferret out elusive
drug suppliers.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:55.229
Presumably, the plot of 24 Jump Street would
be much in the same vein, and would exist

00:01:55.229 --> 00:01:59.450
in the same universe as the existing Jump
Street films, functioning as a continuation

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:03.340
of the story started by officers Morton Schmidt
and Greg Jenko in the first movie.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:07.120
This time, the stars at the center of the
Jump Street tale will reportedly be Tiffany

00:02:07.139 --> 00:02:11.860
Haddish and Zendaya, whom we assume will both
be playing undercover narcotics officers,

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.620
similar to Tatum and Hill's characters in
the first two movies.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:18.580
After directing the first two Jump Street
films, Chris Miller and Phil Lord will be

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:22.850
stepping aside for this third outing, and
Rodney Rothman is coming aboard to helm the

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:26.340
spinoff, collaborating on the script with
Bob's Burgers writers Lizzie and Wendy Molyneux.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:31.500
Rothman previously helped write the screenplay
for 22 Jump Street, and co-directed Lord and

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.820
Miller's acclaimed animated film Spider-Man:
Into the Spider-Verse.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.240
No word yet on what the plot will entail,
or whether Schmidt or Jenko will make an appearance.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.460
Start your engines, because it sounds like
a sequel to 2017's motor-tastic heist hit

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.420
Baby Driver may eventually be zooming its
way into production.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.790
According to Ansel Elgort, the star of the
first film, not only is writer/director Edgar

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:55.990
Wright eager to make a sequel, but he has
in fact already penned the script, and Elgort

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:56.520
has read it.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.260
"Yes, I think it's going to happen.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.200
I think there will be a Baby Driver 2.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:01.980
It has a different title, actually."

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.430
As for what the plot of a Baby Driver sequel
would look like, Wright told Empire in 2017:

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:11.500
"[With] most sequels, you have to contrive
something so they go back to square one, unless

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.160
there's somewhere deeper for them to go.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:16.800
I think with Baby Driver there's more that
you can do in that realm, and I sort of have

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.560
an idea that if you did another one you would
subvert his involvement in the crime in a

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.480
different way so he's not kind of the apprentice
anymore."

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:27.940
Due to Elgort's and Wright's existing commitments,
it could still be a while before Baby Driver

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:32.060
2 moves into production, but it sounds like
once things do move ahead with the high-speed

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.440
sequel, it'll be worth checking out.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.640
Coming off of the runaway success of 2018's
Crazy Rich Asians, it would have been surprising

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.620
if the opulent film didn't earn a sequel.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.480
In fact, it's getting two.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.020
Based on Kevin Kwan's books of the same names,
China Rich Girlfriend and Rich People Problems

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:51.400
are both moving ahead at Warner Bros., although
it may be a while before we get to see them.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.340
Due to the busy schedules of the franchise's
A-list cast and director Jon M. Chu, who is

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:00.910
currently working on adapting Lin-Manuel Miranda's
musical In the Heights for the big screen,

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:04.360
there may be a wait before everyone can get
together again for the next two installments

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.820
in the Crazy Rich Asians saga.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:10.900
However, producer Nina Jacobson says that
the plan is to shoot both sequels back-to-back,

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.050
so that fans aren't waiting years between
the second and third films.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:15.040
Jacobson promises:

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:18.200
"We'll make it up to them on the back end
by shooting two films together."

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:22.360
As for when this back-to-back shooting might
happen, it could still be a ways off.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.230
According to actress Gemma Chan, who portrayed
polished socialite Astrid Leong, filming on

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:31.590
China Rich Girlfriend and Rich People Problems
will begin sometime in, quote, "2020 at the

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:36.780
earliest," making the soonest we can expect
China Rich Girlfriend late 2021, or possibly

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:37.480
even later.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:42.460
While Quentin Tarantino continues to circle
his own eventual R-rated Star Trek spin-off,

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:47.150
Noah Hawley will be reportedly be continuing
the story that began with J.J. Abrams' 2009

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:52.260
outing, centered around Captain James T. Kirk
and the crew of the Enterprise NCC-1701.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:56.850
Hawley, who is best known for the acclaimed
TV series Fargo and Legion, has been tapped

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:00.960
to write and direct a fourth film in the rebooted
Star Trek franchise, continuing the adventures

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:04.380
of Kirk, Spock, Uhura [oo-HOO-ruh], Scotty,
Sulu, and Bones.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:09.020
"You have any idea how ridiculous it is to
hide a starship on the bottom of the ocean?

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:10.600
We've been down here since last night."

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:14.900
Sadly missing from the cast lineup for the
fourth Star Trek film is Anton Yelchin, who

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:19.020
played ship's navigator Pavel Chekov in the
first three rebooted Star Trek films.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:24.440
After completing his work on Star Trek: Beyond,
Yelchin was tragically killed in a 2016 freak

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:27.880
accident in his own driveway, at only 27 years
old.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.340
Since Beyond was already close to release
at the time of his death, Yelchin's storyline

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:36.610
didn't lay any groundwork for him to exit
the franchise, and the film was released largely

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:40.280
unaltered, save for a card at the end that
read simply, "For Anton."

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:45.340
Producer J.J. Abrams has said that the role
of Chekov will not be recast for future Star

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:49.550
Trek films, which means that if and when Hawley's
Star Trek moves into production, it will have

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:53.120
to reckon with the absence of a character
who ended the third film with every intent

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:53.880
of returning.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.020
We appear to be in the midst of an Eddie Murphy
renaissance.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:01.680
After gradually fading from the spotlight
since his heyday in the '80s and early '90s,

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:06.230
Murphy is suddenly back in a big way, giving
a critically acclaimed performance in 2019's

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:10.910
Dolemite Is My Name, making a triumphant return
to Saturday Night Live as a host, lining up

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:15.290
new standup comedy specials for Netflix, and
announcing sequels to two of his biggest hits

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:18.260
from the '80s, Coming to America and Beverly
Hills Cop.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:22.360
Marking the fourth installment in the Beverly
Hills Cop franchise, this newest sequel will

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:26.610
also be a collaboration between Murphy and
Netflix, after Paramount previously pulled

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:30.140
the plug on a planned Beverly Hills Cop 4
back in 2016.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:34.680
Murphy will be reprising his role as Axel
Foley, the Detroit cop who repeatedly finds

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.980
himself traveling to Beverly Hills to investigate
various crimes.

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:43.240
The first Beverly Hills Cop was a smash success
at the box office in 1984, rising to become

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:48.600
one of the highest-grossing comedies of all
time, although the sequels in 1987 and 1994

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.200
brought in diminishing returns.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:54.260
There's no word yet on when Beverly Hills
Cop 4 will move into production at Netflix,

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:58.360
but considering how fast Murphy's star is
once again rising, we wouldn't be surprised

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:01.280
if the streaming giant decides to strike while
the iron is hot.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.760
After six successful installments in the found-footage
horror franchise, Paranormal Activity is coming

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:10.720
back with a seventh film, which will once
again partner Paramount Studios with horror

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.360
mega-producer Jason Blum.

00:07:12.669 --> 00:07:16.940
Although Paranormal Activity 7 has yet to
settle on a director, cast, or title, the

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:20.860
studio has managed to peg down a release date:
March 19, 2021.

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:25.620
The studio is also keeping the story details
under wraps, but with six existing films already

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:30.010
in the franchise, we can take some educated
guesses about what a seventh Paranormal Activity

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:30.940
might look like.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:35.300
After the first film focused on newlyweds
Katie and Micah, every subsequent installment

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.980
has tied back to Katie and her family in one
way or another.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:41.760
Some provide information on Katie and her
sister Kristi's childhood encounters with

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:45.320
a demon, while others detail what happened
to Katie following the events of the first

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:45.820
movie.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:50.400
However, the Paranormal Activity sequels most
frequently focus on new characters that happen

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:54.690
to encounter Katie and her demonic companion,
Tobi, enabling the franchise to tell wider

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:56.780
and more intricately intertwined stories.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:07:59.120
"Hi Tobi."

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:09.680
We expect Paranormal Activity 7 to continue
this trend in some way, introducing a new

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:13.580
group of characters doomed to have their lives
ruined by crossing paths with Katie or her

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:14.080
family.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:18.639
Keeping with the style of the first six films,
we also anticipate the seventh Paranormal

00:08:18.639 --> 00:08:23.370
Activity to be presented as found footage
recorded via security cameras, mobile devices,

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:24.980
and other household recording equipment.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:29.860
Nearly a quarter century after the first Scream
slashed its way into theaters, a fifth installment

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:34.550
in the deliciously self-aware horror franchise
is in the early stages of development at Spyglass

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:35.160
Media Group.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:40.520
The original Scream, released in 1996, was
the brainchild of horror visionary Wes Craven,

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:45.140
who passed away in 2015, and Dawson's Creek
scribe Kevin Williamson.

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:49.460
The screenplay is a near-perfect blend of
meta humor and genuine scares, with its cast

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:53.770
of horror movie aficionados frequently contrasting
how characters in a horror movie would act

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:55.200
versus how they should act.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:09:00.000
"There are certain rules that one must abide
by in order to successfully survive a horror

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:00.500
movie."

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:05.040
The film has since spawned three sequels,
with the most recent, Scream 4, releasing

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:05.800
in 2011.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:10.111
Although Spyglass hasn't announced any details
about the fifth Scream film other than that

00:09:10.111 --> 00:09:14.110
it's happening, chances seem high that the
cast would include original stars Neve Campbell,

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:18.680
Courteney Cox, and David Arquette, who have
appeared in all four previous Scream installments.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:23.310
Up until now, every Scream movie has centered
around Campbell's character, Sidney Prescott,

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:27.510
who has the terrible luck of being repeatedly
targeted by a rotating carousel of killers

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:29.140
donning Ghostface masks.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.240
While it's possible Scream 5 could move away
from Sidney and focus on someone new, we'd

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:36.930
hope that Campbell would be involved in at
least some capacity, along with some of the

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.300
other familiar faces from the previous Scream
movies.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:44.560
Fans of the gibberish-speaking, banana-loving
henchmen of the Despicable Me movies, rejoice!

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:49.620
A sequel to 2015's spinoff film Minions, centered
on the adventures of the tiny terrors, is

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:52.220
set to arrive in theaters on July 3, 2020.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:56.620
This one will be called Minions: The Rise
of Gru, suggesting that we may be getting

00:09:56.620 --> 00:10:00.991
an origin story for the Steve Carell-voiced
protagonist of the Despicable Me movies, from

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.420
the perspective of his most loyal accomplices.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:07.600
Minions, of course, provided audiences with
the backstory for the minions themselves,

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:11.770
and first introduced them to Gru as a child,
so it would make sense for the sequel to pick

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:15.080
up where that film left off, tracing Gru's
path to supervillainy.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:19.600
Returning for The Rise of Gru is director
Kyle Balda, who previously co-directed both

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.390
Minions and Despicable Me 3.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:25.830
However, Pierre Coffin, who co-directed every
previous Despicable Me film on top of voicing

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:30.060
all the minions, will be stepping away from
the co-directorial chair for Rise of Gru,

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:31.680
and will be replaced by Brad Ableson.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:36.100
Never fear, though, Coffin will still be providing
the distinctive voices for the film's beloved

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.120
yellow characters.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:45.940
Steve Carell will likely also be returning,
given the Gru-centric title, but less clear

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:50.380
is whether Sandra Bullock and Jon Hamm will
be reprising their villainous roles from Minions.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:51.000
We hope so.

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:54.280
Even if they're not the main focus, it would
be fun to check in with the Overkills and

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:56.560
see what dastardly things they're up to.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.680
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:02.720
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies and TV shows are coming soon.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:06.380
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

